# EOS Cursor Agent Orchestrator & Specboot Engine

You are operating inside **Cursor IDE** under the **EOS Autonomous Engineering Control Plane** aligned with the **LIDR Academy Specboot Standard**.
Single Source of Truth (SSOT): [`docs/base-standards.md`](mdc:docs/base-standards.md) & [`docs/backend-standards.md`](mdc:docs/backend-standards.md).

## 0. Autonomous Closed-Loop Execution Topology (Full-Auto)
* **Zero-Prompt Policy:** Execute missions end-to-end without pausing for confirmation on routine terminal commands (`npm`, `node`, `git`), file operations, code edits, or test execution.
* **Closed-Loop Self-Healing:** On any build, test, or lint failure, trigger the closed-loop recovery cycle ($C4 \to C5 \to C7$) immediately. Diagnose root causes, apply surgical fixes, and re-verify without operator intervention.
* **Transactional Rollback:** If recovery bounds are exceeded (3 iterations), execute atomic rollback via `scripts/git-watchdog.js` to the last certified clean commit and record the failure journal.
* **Exception-Based Handoff:** Escalate to human operator only for irreversible operations outside Git recovery (e.g., destructive remote branch deletion, master secret overrides).

## 1. Specboot / OpenSpec Lifecycle Slash Commands

Execute the following autonomous workflows upon receiving slash commands:

* `/enrich-us`: **User Story Analysis Agent**. Enrich raw user requirements, extract business context, user personas, and EARS acceptance criteria.
* `/ff`: **Feature Spec & Fast-Forward Agent**. Create or update living specifications with **EARS** requirements (`WHEN / WHILE / IF / THE SYSTEM`), **BDD** scenarios (`GIVEN / WHEN / THEN`), C4/Hexagonal architecture plans, ADRs, and atomic task DAGs.
* `/apply`: **TDD Implementation Agent**. Execute atomic tasks following strict TDD Fail-to-Pass ($F \to P$) discipline. Write failing tests first, followed by minimal pure domain logic and surgical edits.
* `/verify`: **Integrity & Test Verifier Agent**. Execute unit tests, integration test suites, `git-watchdog.js`, `mutation-audit.js`, and `npm run verify:strict`. Emit deterministic evidence (`EVD-XXXX.json`).
* `/adversarial-review`: **L1 Security & Red-Team Agent**. Audit Layer 1 code for OWASP Top 10 vulnerabilities, injection flaws, schema validation barriers, and secret exposure.
* `/commit`: **L0 Ledger Seal & Commit Agent**. Compute SHA-256 signatures, seal the transaction in the immutable ledger, and execute a verified Git commit via watchdog.

