## 2. Complementary Diagnostic & Governance Commands

* `/spec <feature>`: Formalize requirements into EARS syntax and BDD criteria.
* `/tier <task>`: Classify task risk into **Tier 1 (4-step)**, **Tier 2 (8-step)**, or **Tier 3 (21-step)**.
* `/tdd <component>`: Initialize the Red-Green-Refactor test cycle ($F \to P$).
* `/heal`: Activate the Closed-Loop TDD Auto-Healer (max 3 bounded attempts).
* `/drift`: Compare AST of active code against `spec.md` to verify parity.
* `/audit`: Concurrently execute the 7 specialized quality auditors.
* `/cost`: Analyze token expenditure receipt in USD.
* `/c4`: Render interactive C4 and Hexagonal component diagrams in Mermaid.
* `/mutate`: Execute the Mutation Testing Engine (`mutation-audit.js`).
* `/trace`: Generate full requirement-to-evidence proof graph with SHA-256 certificate.
* `/sentinel`: Audit core file signatures and execute FDIR self-healing.
* `/chaos`: Execute adversarial chaos vectors to certify system resilience.
* `/learn`: Extract developmental friction and synthesize Heuristic Learning Deltas.
* `/hud`: Display Live Cockpit HUD in terminal with real-time telemetry.
* `/guardrail`: Inspect pre-tool inputs for injections and post-tool outputs for secret leaks.
* `/otel`: Export OpenInference / OTel semantic telemetry and trace graphs.
* `/checkpoint`: Create atomic restore points with auto-rollback on regression.

